{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/110321-milestone-railroad","id":110321,"title":"Milestone Railroad","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-10T14:58:39-07:00","id":110321,"title":"Milestone Railroad","content":"I've been reading the Promethean Supplements and I began to wonder if writing out a campaigns worth of milestones for session 1 is the best idea. I do think the concept of Milestones is a good one and having a general idea of what they might end up being can be useful. But isn't using them by the book a bit limiting when you have their whole arc planned from day one, what happens if they pick a different direction? Why do they have to develop along certain lines? The books talk about epic journeys. As long as you keep learning shouldn't you accumulate Vitriol? For each session plan some things that will trigger milestones but why do that for the entire story? And when they do something unexpected let the Vitriol condense within them, a lesson learned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/801-grytorm","name":"Grytorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T14:44:14-07:00","id":119978,"title":"","content":"You could handle milestones as you describe - the players don't need to know that you are just giving out milestones based on their roleplaying. That said, I would still use refinement milestones and try to base their milestones on their current refinement to some extent. The prometheans' refinement is their lens for becoming human and thus it should have some influence over milestones.<br /> <br /> Other notes for milestones... IMHO every promethean should have to (at least once):<br /> <br /> 1. Change their refinement<br /> 2. Successfully create a new promethean (not a batch of pandorans)<br /> 3. Choose an athanor<br /> <br /> Of course it's your game and you should do as you wish - but that's my two cents on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}